From ae5c1517b6cbbe73936a2bf38ece341c76136351 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 9 Jul 2026 10:45:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add Concrete-Autoencoder band-selection baseline
 (ConcreteSelect)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Add a Concrete Autoencoder (Balin et al., ICML 2019) baseline for the
learnable band gate, as a controlled comparison for SpecGate: same
band_gate slot, same tau schedule, same selected_bands.json logging and
deploy export — the only variable is the relaxation of the discrete
choice (concrete/Gumbel-softmax selector nodes vs. hard top-k + STE).

- model/modules.py: new ConcreteSelect module with the same
  forward / set_progress / selected_bands API as DiagonalBandGate.
  Training uses k Concrete selector nodes (soft max-over-nodes mask);
  inference takes per-node argmax with collision fill-up so exactly k
  distinct bands are kept (hard k-hot, same exact-pruning deploy path).
- model/model.py: _build_band_gate dispatches on band_select_type
  ("topk" default | "concrete") into the same band_gate slot.
- configs/concrete_k3.yaml: identical to gate_k3.yaml except
  band_select_type: "concrete", so the ablation is confound-free.
- scripts/run_gate_batch.py: new --concrete flag adds a concrete arm
  per (k, seed); comparison plots include it when runs exist.
- run_gate_batch.sh / README.md: document the new baseline and the
  paired multi-seed run recipe.

Verified: config loads and diffs against gate_k3 only in the selector
type; ConcreteSelect train/eval forward, tau anneal, gradient flow and
collision fill-up (20k randomized cases) pass; full
build_model -> forward -> get_selected_bands pipeline runs with
concrete_k3.yaml.

